WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.739
You may have noticed this week that

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.449
your gas prices have gone up.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.529
I want to talk to you a little bit

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.389
about why a lot of it has to

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.440
do with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.849
The White House is trying to blame

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.909
record high gas prices on Russian

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.739
President Vladimir Putin and

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.179
the invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.099
Defending freedom is going to cost.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.019
It's going to cost us as well

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.189
in the United States.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.959
Facing collapsing approval ratings.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.819
Democratic lawmakers are echoing

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.809
the same argument.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.639
New York Congressman Gregory Meeks

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.109
announced that Americans should be

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.359
happy to make that kind of sacrifice

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.429
because in the long run, democracy

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.269
is at stake.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.159
Even simpatico comedians are

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.019
pushing the idea that gas prices

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.939
are setting new highs because of

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.438
world events

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.059
Since the invasion, oil prices have

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.379
skyrocketed today.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.359
The average gas price in America

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.339
hit an all time record high of over

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.939
$4 per gallon.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.789
OK, that stings, but

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.649
a clean conscience is worth

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.209
a buck or two.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.380
I'm willing to pay.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:00.920
Important.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.539
It's important I'm willing to pay

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.439
four dollars a gallon.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.359
Hell, I'll pay fifteen dollars

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.699
a gallon because I drive a Tesla.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.169
The sanctions that the U.S.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.429
and most of Europe have levied

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.839
against Russia, one of the world's

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.729
largest oil producers were

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.589
of course, going to spook energy

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.479
markets. But the so-called Putin

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.429
price hike actually started

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.599
over a year ago.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.759
Biden can't pin our eight percent

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.679
across the board inflation rate, the

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.689
likes of which was last seen early

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.939
in Ronald Reagan's first term,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.529
entirely on Putin.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.939
The main culprit is the massive

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.829
infusion of money into the economy

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.299
by the federal government and the

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.649
Federal Reserve.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.999
Spending in Washington alone

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.429
increased 50 percent between 2019

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.749
and 2021.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.609
On both Biden's and Donald Trump's

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.589
watch, it's a surefire way

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.629
to boost the cost of everything

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.669
as more dollars chase basically

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.139
the same amount of goods.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.369
And when it comes to energy.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.929
Specifically, the Biden

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.669
administration has pursued a number

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.709
of policies designed to make it more

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.509
expensive to produce fossil fuel

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.429
energy in an effort to reach a goal

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.349
of net zero carbon emissions

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.519
by 2050.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.439
In fact, environmentalists cheered

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.329
Biden's bold move a week

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.579
into his presidency as the most

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.799
remarkable day in the history

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.659
of America's official response to

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.679
the climate crisis.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.239
They said it marked the official

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.009
beginning of the end of the fossil

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.089
fuel era.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.679
Biden's measures have included

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.419
halting new permits for drilling and

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.219
leases on federal lands, shutting

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.779
down the planned Keystone XL

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.639
pipeline and proposing the end

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.499
of tax credits for new drilling and

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.969
exploration projects.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.379
He's been joined by congressional

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.879
Democrats have been working to

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.739
tighten regulations loosened during

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.179
the Trump years and otherwise

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.599
clamped down on oil producers.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.569
At the state level, they

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.509
banned fracking in New York in 2014,

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.279
and California has effectively

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.319
stopped the practice in anticipation

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.999
of a 2024 ban.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.379
Even when such moves have been

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.509
overturned by courts are only affect

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.459
future operations, Biden

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.109
and the Democrats have sent a loud

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.939
and clear signal that the future

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.799
will be green, even

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.749
if renewable sources aren't up to

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.759
the task of supplying our energy

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.859
needs. Currently, less than 13

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.659
percent of our energy comes from

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.789
renewable sources, and even as wind,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.649
solar, hydroelectric and other

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.539
sustainable sources do get cheaper

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.519
and more reliable, we're a long

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.559
way from independance on fossil

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.560
fuels.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.369
If patriotism is the last refuge

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.049
of a scoundrel, Biden is blaming

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.059
Putin for the predictable results

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.069
of his and Trump's irresponsible

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:29.879
policies.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.259
If we can't expect lower fuel

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.239
prices, we can at least demand

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.039
an honest accounting of this most

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.589
insidious form of taxation.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.359
Printing money to pay for federal

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.339
largesse with the bill coming

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.529
due at the gas pump, the grocery

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.419
store and just about

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.420
everywhere else.

